translation:
The perfection of generosity, the perfection of ethical discipline, the perfection of patience, the perfection of diligence, the perfection of meditative concentration, and the perfection of wisdom;
Inner emptiness, outer emptiness, inner and outer emptiness, the emptiness of emptiness, great emptiness, the emptiness of the ultimate, the emptiness of the conditioned, the emptiness of the unconditioned, the emptiness of that which transcends limits, the emptiness of that without beginning or end, the emptiness of non-repudiation, the emptiness of nature, the emptiness of all phenomena, the emptiness of specific characteristics, the emptiness of non-apprehension, the emptiness of non-entities, the emptiness of essential nature, and the emptiness of the essential nature of non-entities;
The four foundations of mindfulness, the four correct exertions, the four legs of miraculous power, the five faculties, the five powers, the seven branches of enlightenment, the eightfold noble path, the four noble truths, the four meditative concentrations, the four immeasurables, the four formless absorptions, the eight liberations, and the nine successive absorptions;
The gateways to liberation of emptiness, signlessness, and wishlessness, the five clairvoyances, the concentrations, the gateways of dhāraṇī, the ten powers of the Tathāgata, and the explanation of the meaning of liberation, O Śāradvatīputra;
The purity of form, the purity of feeling, the purity of perception, the purity of compositional factors, the purity of consciousness, the purity of the eye, the purity of the ear, the purity of the nose, the purity of the tongue, the purity of the body, and the purity of the mind;
Furthermore, Subhūti, through the complete purity of form, there is the complete purity of sound; through the complete purity of sound, there is the complete purity of odor; through the complete purity of odor, there is the complete purity of taste; through the complete purity of taste, there is the complete purity of touch; through the complete purity of touch, there is the complete purity of phenomena;
And through the complete purity of phenomena, there is the complete purity of eye-consciousness, up to the complete purity of mind-consciousness.
